              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#CategoricalSemanticsOfWTypesReferences"}
                    Categorical semantics of
                    = succeed "-types" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒲
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{W}
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            An
            %strong
              initial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+for+an+endofunctor"} algebra
            for an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            in the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+endofunctor"} algebras
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+types"} inductive types
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_algebras_over_a_monad Relation to algebras over a monad
          %p
            The concept of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+an+endofunctor"} algebra of an endofunctor
            is arguably somewhat odd, a more natural concept being that of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebra over a monad
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+category"} complete category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+an+endofunctor"} algebras of an endofunctor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{C}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+a+monad"} algebras over a monad
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+monad"} free monad
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            The proof is fairly straightforward, see for instance (
            %a{:href => "#Maciej"}> Maciej
            ) or at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+monad"} free monad
          %p
            The existence of free monads, on the other hand, can be a tricky question. One general technique is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+construction+of+free+algebras"} transfinite construction of free algebras
          %h3#LambeksTheorem Lambek’s theorem
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              has an initial algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo :
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha: F(X) \to X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X)
              via
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In this sense,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %em smallest
              fixed point of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              in that there is a map from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to any other fixed point (indeed, any other algebra), and this map is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The dual concept is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+coalgebra"} terminal coalgebra
              %em largest
              fixed point of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Given an initial algebra structure
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo :
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha: F(X) \to X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X)
              to be
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\alpha): F(F(X)) \to F(X)
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: X \to F(X)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi i
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi α
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi α
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    F(X) &amp; \overset{F(i)}{\to} &amp; F(F(X)) \\
                    \\alpha \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow F(\alpha) \\
                    X &amp; \underset{i}{\to} &amp; F(X)
                    }
            %p
              commutes. Now it is trivial, in fact tautological that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              is itself an
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X) \to X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \circ i = 1_X
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is initial. As a result,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\alpha) \circ F(i) = 1_{F(X)}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi α
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \circ \alpha = 1_{F(X)}
              according to the commutative square. Hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              is an isomorphism, with inverse
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          %h3#AdameksTheorem-sec Adámek’s theorem
          %p
            In many cases, initial algebras can be constructed in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/recursion"} recursive/iterative
            fashion using
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ad%C3%A1mek%27s+fixed+point+theorem"} Adámek's fixed point theorem
          %h3#semantics_for_inductive_types Semantics for inductive types
          %p
            Initial algebras of endofunctors provide
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+type+theory"} extensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+types"} inductive types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+initial"} weak initial
            algebras captures the notion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional type theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#NaturalNumbers Natural numbers
          %p
            The archetypical example of an initial algebra is the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \mathcal{T} \to \mathcal{T}
              the functor given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F : X \mapsto * \coprod X
            %p
              (i.e. the functor underlying the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maybe+monad"}> maybe monad
              ”). Then an initial algebra over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is precisely a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number+object"} natural number object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By definition, an
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              equipped with a morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (0,s) :  * \coprod X \to X
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence equivalently with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 : * \to X
              and an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s : X \to X
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mn 0
                        %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0_Y, s_Y) : * \coprod Y \to Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    * &amp;\stackrel{0}{\to}&amp; X &amp;\stackrel{s}{\to}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    * &amp;\stackrel{0}{\to}&amp; Y &amp;\stackrel{s}{\to}&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              commutes. This is the very definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number+object"} natural number object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \mathbb{N}
          %h3#bipointed_sets Bi-pointed sets
          %p#BiPointedSets
            Another example of an initial algebra is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bi-pointed+set"} bi-pointed set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \mathcal{T} \to \mathcal{T}
              the functor given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F : X \mapsto * \coprod *
            %p
              Then an initial algebra over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is precisely a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bi-pointed+object"} bi-pointed object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
          %h3#more_examples More examples
          %p
            Theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdameksTheorem"}
            applies (in particular) to any functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: Set \to Set
            which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            of finitely
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functors"} representable functors
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(n, -): X \mapsto X^n
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              be a set, and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: Set \to Set
              be the functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X) = 1 + A \times X
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+monoid"} free monoid
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mo ,
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e, m| ): 1 + A \times A^* \to A^*
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e: 1 \to A^*
              is the identity and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m|: A \times A^* \to A^*
              is the restriction of the monoid multiplication along the evident inclusion
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ×
                      %mn 1
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo *
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \times 1: A \times A^* \to A^* \times A^*
            %p
              This “fixed point” of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              can be thought of as the result of the (slightly nonsensical) calculation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mi …
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 + A \times X = X \Rightarrow X = \frac1{1 - A} = 1 + A + A^2 + \ldots = A^*
            %p
              which can be made rigorous by interpreting the initial equality as defining the solution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              by recursion, and applying the theorem above.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: Set \to Set
              be the functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X) = 1 + X^2
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              of isomorphism classes of finite (planar, rooted) binary
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trees"} trees
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r, j): 1 + T^2 \to T
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r: 1 \to T
              names the tree consisting of just a root vertex, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j: T^2 \to T
              creates a tree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi t
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \vee t'
              from two trees
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t'
              by joining their roots to a new root, so that the root of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              becomes the left child and the root of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t'
              the right child of the new root.
            %p The recursive equation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T = 1 + T^2
            %p
              would seem to imply that the structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              behaves something like a structural “sixth root of unity”, and indeed the structural isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \cong F(T)
              allows one to exhibit an isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T = T^7
            %p
              constructively, as famously explored by Andreas Blass in the paper “
              %a{:href => "#BlassSeven"}> Seven trees in one
              ”.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: Set \to Set
              be the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X) = X^*
              (the free monoid from an earlier example). Then the initial
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trees"} trees
              (not necessarily binary as in the previous example).
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coslice+category"} coslice category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mi Ab
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \downarrow Ab
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: C \to C
              be the functor which pushes out along the multiplication-by-
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              map
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \cdot -: \mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pruefer+group"} Pruefer group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[p^{-1}]/\mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2008/11/coalgebraically_thinking.html#c020660"} here
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ban
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ban
              be the category of complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+spaces"} Banach spaces
              and maps of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
              bounded above by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi Ban
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi Ban
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: \mathbb{C} \downarrow Ban \to \mathbb{C} \downarrow Ban
              be the squaring functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto X \times X
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^1([0, 1])
              (with respect to the usual
              = succeed ")." do
